l4e12_thermal.py: layer 4 task L4-E12 (MESHSAT-1478 under MESHSAT-1357). The kit's electronics against the inside air at
D-02a's +55 C operating margin (E3-O) and E5's +60 C dwell in the sealed Peli 1450. Prototype design, desk arithmetic: nothing
is bought, built, powered or measured. Classes: MAKER, MODELED, INFERRED, ASSUMPTION, CONDITIONAL. Revised after the focused
check astra-check-l4e12-1 (B1 to B3 and the minors; the record's section 12 maps each item to its change).

0 Reproductions and inputs
0a pwr_budget.py re-run in a child: pwr_budget.out and pwr_budget.json byte for byte: yes
0b pwr_red2.py re-run in a child: pwr_red2.out byte for byte: yes
0c pwr_red2.py imported here prints pwr_red2.out byte for byte (its heat() and states are the record's): yes
0d grade_check.build() (it writes nothing): 150 fitted lines, 19 modules, 10 lines no grade row covers; its own in-use bar 51 C
0e 63 inputs pinned by sha256 (the list ends this output)

1 The acceptance, read first (quoted)
1a D-02a (owner ruling, 25 September 2026): "TEST-PLAN's +55 C operating, +71 C storage and -33 C storage are QUALIFICATION MARGINS over the -20 to +40 C use and -20 to +45 C storage envelope, with two pass lines: operate to specification inside the envelope; survive and recover at the margin."
1b SC-03 (session choice under the owner's standing rule): "A qualification margin, judged like E3 and E4 under D-02a: survive and recover at the margin, and operate to specification inside the envelope."
1c TEST-PLAN E3 (section 2): "**E3-O** operation 4 hours at +55 C deployed with the monitor and radios on, on shore or vehicle input, as a deviation with the cells kept out of the heat"
   its pass line: "survive and recover (D-02a): no damage, no deformation, no lost data or keys, CM5 throttling logged but no shutdown, and the functional check passes once the kit is back inside the envelope with its pack refitted"
   section 6: "**test deviation**: deployed, monitor and radios on, on shore or vehicle input, the cells kept out of the heat (the arrangement above)"; the deployed state: "deployed (open, antennas on, cables in, pack fitted, shaded, D-02e)"
1d TEST-PLAN E5: 10 cycles of 24 h at 95 % RH, 30 to 60 C, "deployed (lid open; the case has **no vent opening**", "on shore or vehicle input with the kit logging"
   its pass line: "survive and recover (D-02a, SC-03): no condensation inside (inside humidity log), no corrosion, functional check passes"
1e The deviation's arrangement (section 6, E3-O and E5): "the kit's controls read room-temperature cells, so of their temperature triggers only C1's inside-air trigger sheds modules"
1f CONOPS 4: "C1, module shedding | inside air +50 C or any cell +55 C | normal to the reduced mode; reached again in the reduced mode, to the heat stage; restores 5 K below"; the heat stage (after BANK-R1) runs one module carrying the owner's D-02b example (GNSS, the LoRa mesh, Iridium and APRS beacons) with the SOS path, the required set (REQ-052).; it turns off "after BANK-R1: slots 1 and 2, so bank 1 (the SDR, the camera, the QMX, the wall port), the 5G module (its data is slot 2's), both WiFi link cards, the monitor"
1g D-02b (owner ruling): "Closed-lid operation in a defined REDUCED MODE (for example GNSS, the LoRa mesh, Iridium and APRS beacons, monitor off, one CM5); a closed-lid state and thermal test join TEST-PLAN; a lid sensor is an engineering item (the case-open switch can serve both). Accepted consequences: above +35 C ambient the kit runs one module; with three loaded modules charging holds off above about +25 C."
1h REQ-051's acceptance: "Inside the envelope, the functional check (TEST-PLAN section 4) passes at the envelope's limits, the hot and humid limits with the pack fitted (TEST-PLAN E3-A, E5-A). At each margin level, in the state the row names (E3-S and E4-S stored with the pack out; E3-O and E5 as stated deviations, the pack outside the chamber): no damage, no lost data or keys, and full function resumed once the kit is back inside the envelope, with its logs intact. The exposures with the pack fitted (E3-T, E4-T) and the pack's own soaks (E3-P, E4-P) run at its cells' limits (TEST-PLAN section 6). TEST-PLAN states both pass lines, never reports a margin result as an envelope claim, and never reports a deviation's pass as the kit's margin with its pack."
1i What it requires (INFERRED from 1a to 1h): at both margins the kit is to survive and recover; operation to specification
   is required only inside the envelope. E3-O runs four hours at +55 C deployed with the monitor and radios on; the one
   control action its arrangement records is C1's inside-air shedding of modules (1e), which takes the kit to the heat stage
   (1f). Nothing else may turn a radio off in E3-O: the radios C1 leaves on (Iridium, the LoRa mesh, APRS, both E72, GNSS)
   stay on for the four hours, and a further shedding would change E3-O's configuration (no authority: withdrawn from the
   first revision). E5 requires logging, not the radios (1d), so a step of the kit's controls that turns radios off may act
   in E5 and must not act in E3-O. The SGP41 is neither the monitor nor a radio and E3-O's row does not name it; its own
   protective shutdown is inside E3-O's stated configuration (SESSION reading, named for TEST-PLAN's owner). The lid-closed
   mode and EMCON ("radios dark (owner ruling D-05)") change the configuration and are not used. E3-O is taken to start from a kit stabilised at
   the chamber's +55 C, as L4-E10 took it; started straight from E3-S's +71 C soak, the radios would be past +70 C at power-on
   (a sequence item for TEST-PLAN's owner, section 7 of the record).
1j Which limits apply (the corrected rule, SESSION): a powered part, its maker's recommended or operating range, whether it
   must work in the exposure (the CM5, the logging chain, the fans, the radios in E3-O) or is merely powered; an absolute
   maximum is a stress rating only (TLV755P p.4 and PCM2912A p.5, read: "Stresses beyond those listed under Absolute Maximum Ratings may cause permanent " ...) and serves as an
   exclusion screen, never as a statement of no damage; a powered part past its operating range and under its absolute
   maximum is INCONCLUSIVE unless a maker states recovery (Quectel RM520N p.19: "without any unrecoverable malfunction. Radio spectrum and radio networ").
   An unpowered part, its storage range where stated, else its operating range, the only statement held; a duration the maker
   does not state stays open (the SGP41's "short-term"). A part through the plate or the wall: the plate to the inside air.

2 The thermal state at the margins (MODELED unless marked)
2a The heat stage after BANK-R1 (PS-SURV-R) on shore, plan: 23.272 W at the pack, 24.996 W into the case with the front end's and
   charger's loss on the loads; as board B is generated (PS-SURV) 23.345 W. HIGH: 50.423 W (not covered, as L4-E10 and LO-01a).
2b T-H1's floor (LO-01a): the inside air at or under the SGP41's +55 C (MAKER, p.7 Table 5) at +40 C on shore: 1.6664 W/K;
   L4-E10's printed 1.6664 W/K, 70.00 and 75.00 C agree: yes (70.00, 75.00 C uncond.)
2c L4-E8's ballasts, 2.09 W at the bound's worst corner (MODELED by L4-E8, cited from L4-E9 IF-08): +1.254 K. The inside air
   (mixed) at the floor:
   E3-O 71.25 C, E5's dwell 76.25 C (steady; a 4 h E3-O from a kit at +55 C reaches 69.78 to 70.44 C at 32.53's 10 to 8 kJ/K,
   so the steady air is the bound; E5's 6 h dwell reaches it). At HIGH heat E5's air would be 91.5 C.
2d A charge running on shore (the pack outside, at room temperature, inside its window): +3.446 W, +2.07 K. E3-O states no
   charge state; the route below keeps E3-O as stated and counts no charge (TEST-PLAN's owner records the pack's state, 7).
2e Inside the envelope at the floor (+40 C, heat stage, ballasts): 56.25 C, over the SGP41's +55 C line of E3-L (REQ-052);
   LO-01a's floor with the ballasts counted is 1.8058 W/K (a finding for L4-E9 and L4-E10, section 7).
2f The plate and the walls (INFERRED from W4's film coefficients, inside 10 to 25, outside face 9.5 to 11.5, wall 8 to 10 W/m2K, wall t/k 0.018):
   the plate sits at the ambient plus 0.465 to 0.725 of the rise, a PP wall's inner face at 0.541 to 0.781 of it.
2g The enclosure (INFERRED, W4, a sensitivity estimate and not a model of the kit): lid open with fans 1.22 (low case) to 2.85
   W/K (high case); 32.53 gives 3.0 to 3.3. With the inside film taken as infinite the outer films give 2.10 W/K in the low
   case and 3.86 W/K in the high case: a cap of the low case's coefficients and areas, not a universal bound. Low outer films
   with W4's high inside film: 1.62 W/K; high outer films with its low inside film: 2.05 W/K.
2h The running module's cooler exhaust (MODELED): the representative 30 mm fan's 3.7 CFM free-air (MAKER, Sunon p.1) at 50 %
   through the heatsink (ASSUMPTION), 0.873 l/s: the CM5's 4.5 W and the fan's 0.51 W lift the exhaust 5.64 K over the mixed air in
   the heat stage, and the idle module's 2.0 W 2.78 K in the hold. A part outside the exhaust sits at the mixed air.
2i The design as it stands (the heat stage at T-H1's floor, the ballasts on):
   E3-O ambient 55.0 C; mixed air 71.25 C; in the exhaust 76.89 C; plate 62.6..66.8 C; PP wall's inner face 63.8..67.7 C
   E5   ambient 60.0 C; mixed air 76.25 C; in the exhaust 81.89 C; plate 67.6..71.8 C; PP wall's inner face 68.8..72.7 C

