3d FINDING, in the envelope as well (the generators' own declarations): board E's U13 is a TLV75533 in SOT-23-5 (DBV, 231.1 C/W,
   recommended junction +125 C, absolute +150 C, MAKER, TLV755P sheet, held back) on a rail declared at 0.35 A typical and 0.60 A
   peak from 5.0 V: 0.595 W, +137.5 K, past its recommended +125 C at any local air above -12.5 C; the declared peak exceeds its 500 mA
   output. Board C's U5 (the same part) is declared 0.149 A typical and 0.720 A peak, the peak past 500 mA. Even at the model's plan
   load U13 passes its recommended junction at both margins (3c): the regulators are part of the route (5c).

4 Three complete approaches for the parts that collide (the same margins, the same floor, the same ballasts, the plan heat)
   Common to all three (none can be done by the air, the physics of 4a): the SGP41's own shutdown (5d); the MAIN, PI and TEST
   pushbuttons to a +85 C part; PDi's storage statement for the e-paper; board E's and board C's 3.3 V regulators (5c); the
   +70 C parts out of the running cooler's exhaust; the fans and the other lines with no range held (7).
4a (a) THE HEAT PATH AND THE ENCLOSURE, no new mode: the heat stage at both margins, the radios on at both. Each part routed by
   the air needs (MODELED, E3-O / E5):
      RB9704    1.806 / 2.709 W/K
      LIME      1.806 / 2.709 W/K
      SA868     1.806 / 2.709 W/K
      PCM2912A  1.806 / 2.709 W/K
      G6K       1.806 / 2.709 W/K
      SGP41     1.806 / 2.709 W/K
      H5007NL   1.806 / 2.709 W/K
      ATP16     1.806 / 2.709 W/K
      PXP4043C  1.806 / 2.709 W/K
      XENARC    1.083 / 1.354 W/K
      CM5       0.903 / 1.083 W/K
      SOUNDER   0.903 / 1.083 W/K
      NVME      0.903 / 1.083 W/K
      AW7915    0.774 / 0.903 W/K
      RM520N    0.774 / 0.903 W/K
   so the line is 2.709 W/K (0 K margin), 3.010 with 1 K and 3.386 with 2 K; E3-O alone 1.806 W/K. It lies over the low case's
   outer-film cap (2.10 W/K) and under W4's high case (2.85 W/K finite inside film, 3.86 infinite); 32.53 gives 3.0 to 3.3.
   Not routed by the air (the air cannot be cooled below the ambient without a cooler, and a cooler in the sealed case returns
   its input to the air, L4-E10's corrected balance):
      ATP19     its limit 55 C (operating range) is at or under E3-O's ambient
      EPAPER    its limit 60 C (operating range (the only statement held)) is at or under E5's ambient
   Coupling the +70 C modules to the plate instead: the plate at E5 is 67.6..71.8 C at the floor; it needs 1.963 W/K at the plate's
   upper fraction, and the parts that cannot be coupled still need the line above. VERDICT: CONDITIONAL on T-H1 at or over
   2.709 W/K; not selected (0.55 W/K over (c)); it is what applies, with no hold, if T-H1 reads at or over it.
4b (b) WIDER-RATED PARTS, the mode and the enclosure unchanged (the inside air 76.25 C at E5, 81.89 C in the exhaust):
      RB9704    OWNER (CHO-001)   no wider-rated Iridium IMT unit in any held document
      LIME      OWNER (CHO-001)   its maker's page offers the commercial grade only (0 to +70 C in use and in storage)
      SA868     OWNER (CHO-001)   no VHF module rated past +70 C in any held document
      PCM2912A  SESSION           its recommended range ends at +70 C; no wider-rated USB audio codec held
      G6K       SESSION           no signal relay rated past +70 C held; an +85 C part is a Layer 6 pick
      SGP41     OWNER (CHO-001)   Bosch BME688 (gas sensing -40 to +85 C, storage -45 to +85 C), already on board E as U14; a second one takes I2C 0x77, which the outside pod's BME688 (32.54, deferred) then cannot use; at E5 3.11 K inside the candidate's +85 C (MAKER)
      H5007NL   SESSION           the maker's HX (extended temperature) version, -40 to +85 C; pin compatibility not claimed; at E5 3.11 K inside the candidate's +85 C (MAKER)
      ATP19     SESSION           NKK MBN sealed pushbutton (IP67, -30 to +85 C); its 12 mm bushing, terminals and cutout are owed; at E5 8.75 K inside the candidate's +85 C (MAKER)
      ATP16     SESSION           NKK MBN sealed pushbutton, as ATP19; at E5 8.75 K inside the candidate's +85 C (MAKER)
      SOUNDER   SESSION           no change: muted, its storage range reaches +85 C; at E5 8.75 K inside the candidate's +85 C (MAKER)
      EPAPER    OWNER (CHO-001)   no e-paper rated past +60 C in any held document
      PXP4043C  SESSION           the same maker's 4000 series sheet states -40 to +80 C for the series; the C-type's own sheet says +70 C; at E5 3.75 K inside the candidate's +80 C (MAKER)
      NVME      SESSION           the pick: a wide grade (Cervoz -40 to +85 C), not the 0 to +70 C standard grade; at E5 3.11 K inside the candidate's +85 C (MAKER)
   VERDICT: not selectable by the session (five device-set parts are the owner's, CHO-001, four with no candidate held).
4c (c) E3-O AS STATED, THE HOLD IN E5 ONLY: in E3-O the heat stage runs with every radio C1 leaves on (no hold); in E5 a step
   of the kit's controls beyond the heat stage holds the charge (as H1), idles the running module (no shutdown) and powers off
   board D (APRS), the PA rail, the RockBLOCK (RB_SW_EN), the LoRa module (LORA_ON), both E72 (ZB_ON) and the Geiger module
   (GEIGER_EN). H1's own actions, which it reuses (CONOPS 4c): "through board A's expanders on the kit bus it turns off the monitor, the pack heater, board D, PoE, the USB-C outlet, the wall port's VBUS and the PA and HF software holds; it holds the charge by the charger's own charge-inhibit bit". Heat in E5 under it: 19.497 W (MODELED,
   plan; 18.152 W at the pack); as board B is generated, the 5G socket's supply dropped too, 19.497 W. Each part routed by the
   air needs (MODELED, E3-O with the heat stage / E5 with the hold):
      RB9704    1.806 / 2.159 W/K
      LIME      1.806 / 2.159 W/K
      SA868     1.806 / 2.159 W/K
      G6K       1.806 / 2.159 W/K
      SGP41     1.806 / 2.159 W/K
      H5007NL   1.806 / 2.159 W/K
      ATP16     1.806 / 2.159 W/K
      PXP4043C  1.806 / 2.159 W/K
      PCM2912A  1.806 / 0.240 W/K
      XENARC    1.083 / 1.079 W/K
      CM5       0.903 / 0.863 W/K
      SOUNDER   0.903 / 0.863 W/K
      NVME      0.903 / 0.863 W/K
      AW7915    0.774 / 0.720 W/K
      RM520N    0.774 / 0.720 W/K
   so the line is G_c = 2.159 W/K, set by E5 (E3-O alone 1.806 W/K); 2.399 with 1 K and 2.698 with 2 K of margin; with the module
   at its typical 4.5 W in the hold 2.443 W/K; at HIGH heat 4.304 W/K (not covered). Over the low case's cap by 0.058 W/K, inside
   W4's range and under 32.53's: CONDITIONAL on T-H1. Not routed by the air:
      ATP19     its limit 55 C (operating range) is at or under E3-O's ambient
      EPAPER    its limit 60 C (operating range (the only statement held)) is at or under E5's ambient
4d THE HOLD'S TRIGGER WINDOW at the line (it must not act in E3-O, and must act in E5 before the radios it turns off pass
   their +70 C): E3-O's steady mixed air with the radios on 67.55 C; the mixed air by which E5 needs the hold 70.00 C; window 2.45 K.
   Taken from it: the reference's error twice (board B's TMP117, +-0.2 C to 100 C, MAKER p.1), E5's fastest rise 15.0 K/h (the
   chamber's 30 to 60 C in 2 h, Method 507.6 as L4-E10 transcribed it) times a 61 s reading and response lag (ASSUMPTION):
   0.25 K. What is left bounds the reference's offset to the air at the +70 C parts: at most +-0.90 K (INFERRED). The TMP117 is
   a board sensor under the coolers: across the exhaust's 0 to 5.64 K the window is -3.84 K, so it DOES NOT EXIST unless the
   reference is placed in the mixed air near those parts or its offset is calibrated at T-H1 to +-0.90 K (CONDITIONAL); with the
   whole spread it would need 3.111 W/K. The trigger then sits at the window's middle, 68.65 C of mixed air plus the calibrated
   offset; restore 5 K under it after 30 minutes (PROVISIONAL). The window grows with the conductance: 2.45 K at 2.159 W/K; 4.17 K at 2.500 W/K; 5.00 K at 2.709 W/K.
   Inside the envelope the air is 52.55 C at the line, far under it. In E5 under the hold the mixed air settles at 70.00 C.
