5d The SGP41's own shutdown, apart from the hold: board E's BME688 (U14, +-0.5 C from 0 to 65 C, MAKER p.14) beside it within
   0.5 K (ASSUMPTION, a placement rule) switches it off at 53.75 C (its +55 C less the error, the gradient and 0.25 K of lag) and
   back on at 50 C (Table 4's recommended maximum, MAKER p.6); off at every start until a reading at or under 50 C, so
   E3-O, which starts from a kit at +55 C, never powers it. Its function is kept for any bay air up to 52.75 C; inside the envelope
   at the line the air is 52.55 C (0.20 K to spare); at T-H1's floor it would be 56.25 C, so there the function is lost at the hot
   edge (finding 1 already fails that floor). Unpowered at the line it sits at 67.5..73.2 C in E3-O and 70.0..72.8 C in E5 against its +70 C
   short-term storage, whose duration Sensirion does not state: CONDITIONAL on its answer, and on a supply switch and a bus of
   its own so that no live pin feeds it.
